From pburns at pburns.seanet.com  Sat Jun  4 18:16:01 2005
From: pburns at pburns.seanet.com (Patrick Burns)
Date: Sat, 04 Jun 2005 19:16:01 +0100
Subject: Re: Find the K largest & smallest entries in a Correlation Matrix
In-Reply-To: <001d01c56918$eb6a7000$98c1b3d1@D6WVZ821>
References: <001d01c56918$eb6a7000$98c1b3d1@D6WVZ821>
Message-ID: <42A1EFE1.8040604@pburns.seanet.com>

You could do something like:

k <- 10
lt.cor <- spcor[lower.tri(spcor, diag=FALSE)]
ltc.sort <- sort(lt.cor)
lower.cor <- ltc.sort[k]
upper.cor <- ltc.sort[length(ltc.sort) - k + 1]

corloc <- array(FALSE, dim(spcor), dimnames(spcor))
corloc[lower.tri(corloc, diag=FALSE)] <- lt.cor <= lower.cor

If S-PLUS has an 'arr.ind' argument in 'which'  like R does,
then you can just do:

which(corloc, arr.ind=TRUE)

